8390 affecting package openssl for versions less than 3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"openssl\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:42.935097+00:00\",\"source\":\"azure_linux\",\"description\":\"CVE-2026-28390 affecting package openssl for versions less than 3.3.5-5. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2026-34757\",\"title\":\"CVE-2026-34757 affecting package libpng for versions less than 1\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libpng\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:42.934758+00:00\",\"source\":\"azure_linux\",\"description\":\"CVE-2026-34757 affecting package libpng for versions less than 1.6.57-1. An upgraded version of the package is available that resolves this issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-70873\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-70873 affecting package sqlite for versions less than 3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"sqlite\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:42.933816+00:00\",\"source\":\"azure_linux\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-70873 affecting package sqlite for versions less than 3.44.0-3. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-12404\",\"title\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libgcrypt\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:40.105112+00:00\",\"source\":\"alibaba_linux\",\"description\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2.1903 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\\n\\nCVE-2018-0495:\\nLibgcrypt before 1.7.10 and 1.8.x before 1.8.3 allows a memory-cache side-channel attack on ECDSA signatures that can be mitigated through the use of blinding during the signing process in the _gcry_ecc_ecdsa_sign function in cipher/ecc-ecdsa.c, aka the Return Of the Hidden Number Problem or ROHNP. To discover an ECDSA key, the attacker needs access to either the local machine or a different virtual machine o\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-0495\",\"title\":\"Libgcrypt\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libgcrypt\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:40.105070+00:00\",\"source\":\"alibaba_linux\",\"description\":\"Libgcrypt before 1.7.10 and 1.8.x before 1.8.3 allows a memory-cache side-channel attack on ECDSA signatures that can be mitigated through the use of blinding during the signing process in the _gcry_ecc_ecdsa_sign function in cipher/ecc-ecdsa.c, aka the Return Of the Hidden Number Problem or ROHNP. To discover an ECDSA key, the attacker needs access to either the local machine or a different virtual machine on the same physical host.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-15473\",\"title\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"openssh\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:40.100081+00:00\",\"source\":\"alibaba_linux\",\"description\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2.1903 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\\n\\nCVE-2018-15473:\\nOpenSSH through 7.7 is prone to a user enumeration vulnerability due to not delaying bailout for an invalid authenticating user until after the packet containing the request has been fully parsed, related to auth2-gss.c, auth2-hostbased.c, and auth2-pubkey.c.\\n  \"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-12697\",\"title\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"binutils\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:40.095763+00:00\",\"source\":\"alibaba_linux\",\"description\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2.1903 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\\n\\nCVE-2018-1000876:\\nbinutils version 2.32 and earlier contains a Integer Overflow vulnerability in objdump, bfd_get_dynamic_reloc_upper_bound,bfd_canonicalize_dynamic_reloc that can result in Integer overflow trigger heap overflow. Successful exploitation allows execution of arbitrary code.. This attack appear to be exploitable via Local. This vulnerability appears to have been fixed in after commit 3a551c7a1b80fca57946177486\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-1000876\",\"title\":\"binutils version 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"binutils\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:40.095679+00:00\",\"source\":\"alibaba_linux\",\"description\":\"binutils version 2.32 and earlier contains a Integer Overflow vulnerability in objdump, bfd_get_dynamic_reloc_upper_bound,bfd_canonicalize_dynamic_reloc that can result in Integer overflow trigger heap overflow. Successful exploitation allows execution of arbitrary code.. This attack appear to be exploitable via Local. This vulnerability appears to have been fixed in after commit 3a551c7a1b80fca579461774860574eabfd7f18f.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-18311\",\"title\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"perl\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:40.091775+00:00\",\"source\":\"alibaba_linux\",\"description\":\"Package updates are available for Alibaba Cloud Linux 2.1903 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\\n\\nCVE-2018-18311:\\nPerl before 5.26.3 and 5.28.x before 5.28.1 has a buffer overflow via a crafted regular expression that triggers invalid write operations.\\n  \"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2022-22824\",\"title\":\"Security fix for expat in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"expat\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.356853+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for expat in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2022-22823\",\"title\":\"Security fix for expat in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"expat\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.356801+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for expat in Alpine Li