E-2018-5736\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333257+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-5737\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333229+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2017-3145\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333196+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2017-3138\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333129+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2017-3137\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333098+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2017-3136\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333073+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2016-9444\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333046+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2016-9147\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.333018+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2016-9131\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bind\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.332990+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bind in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2016-0634\",\"title\":\"Security fix for bash in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:24.332926+00:00\",\"source\":\"alpine\",\"description\":\"Security fix for bash in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2011-4578\",\"title\":\"event\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acpid\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.010971+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"event.c in acpid (aka acpid2) before 2.0.11 does not have an appropriate umask setting during execution of event-handler scripts, which might allow local users to (1) perform write operations within directories created by a script, or (2) read files created by a script, via standard filesystem system calls.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2011-2777\",\"title\":\"samples/powerbtn/powerbtn\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acpid\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.010883+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"samples/powerbtn/powerbtn.sh in acpid (aka acpid2) 2.0.16 and earlier uses the pidof program incorrectly, which allows local users to gain privileges by running a program with the name kded4 and a DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS environment variable containing commands.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2011-1159\",\"title\":\"acpid\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acpid\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.010803+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"acpid.c in acpid before 2.0.9 does not properly handle a situation in which a process has connected to acpid.socket but is not reading any data, which allows local users to cause a denial of service (daemon hang) via a crafted application that performs a connect system call but no read system calls.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2009-4235\",\"title\":\"acpid 1\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acpid\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.010719+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"acpid 1.0.4 sets an unrestrictive umask, which might allow local users to leverage weak permissions on /var/log/acpid, and obtain sensitive information by reading this file or cause a denial of service by overwriting this file, a different vulnerability than CVE-2009-4033.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2009-4033\",\"title\":\"A certain Red Hat patch for acpid 1\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acpid\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.010639+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"A certain Red Hat patch for acpid 1.0.4 effectively triggers a call to the open function with insufficient arguments, which might allow local users to leverage weak permissions on /var/log/acpid, and obtain sensitive information by reading this file, cause a denial of service by overwriting this file, or gain privileges by executing this file.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2009-0798\",\"title\":\"ACPI Event Daemon (acpid)\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acpid\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.010547+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"ACPI Event Daemon (acpid) before 1.0.10 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption and connectivity loss) by opening a large number of UNIX sockets without closing them, which triggers an infinite loop.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2009-4411\",\"title\":\"The (1) setfacl and (2) getfacl commands in XFS acl 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"acl\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-29T03:32:22.009822+00:00\",\"source\":\"debian\",\"description\":\"The (1) setfacl and (2) getfacl commands in XFS acl 2.2.47, when running in recursive (-R) mode, follow symbolic links even when the --physical (aka -P) or -L option is specified, which might allow local users to modify the ACL for arbitrary files or directories via a symlink attack.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-40087\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-40087 affecting package kernel for versions less than 6\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"kernel\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-28T11:16:29.952805+00:00\",\"source\":\"azure_linux\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-40087 affecting package kernel for versions less than 6.6.117.1-1. An upgraded version of the package is available that resolves this issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-40096\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-40096 affecting package kernel for versions less than 6\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"kernel\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-28T11:16:29.952739+00:00\",\"source\":\"azure_linux\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-40096 affecting package kernel for versions less than 6.6.117.1-1. An upgraded version of the package is available that resolves this issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-40100\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-40100 affecting package kernel for versions less than 6\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"kernel\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-28T11:16:29.952673+00:00\",\"source\":\"azure_linux\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-40100 affecting package kernel for versions less than 6.6.117.1-1. An upgraded version of the package is available that resolves this issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-202