627+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libxml2 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2022-2309\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libxml2 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libxml2\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:05.604588+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libxml2 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2020-8252\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libuv in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libuv\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:05.603534+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libuv in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2021-46848\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libtasn1\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:05.603379+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2022-3715\",\"title\":\"A flaw was found in the bash package, where a heap-buffer overflow can occur in valid parameter_tran...\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463690+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"A flaw was found in the bash package, where a heap-buffer overflow can occur in valid parameter_transform. This issue may lead to memory problems.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2019-9924\",\"title\":\"rbash in Bash\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463632+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"rbash in Bash before 4.4-beta2 did not prevent the shell user from modifying BASH_CMDS, thus allowing the user to execute any command with the permissions of the shell.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2019-18276\",\"title\":\"An issue was discovered in disable_priv_mode in shell\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463570+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"An issue was discovered in disable_priv_mode in shell.c in GNU Bash through 5.0 patch 11. By default, if Bash is run with its effective UID not equal to its real UID, it will drop privileges by setting its effective UID to its real UID. However, it does so incorrectly. On Linux and other systems that support \\\"saved UID\\\" functionality, the saved UID is not dropped. An attacker with command execution in the shell can use \\\"enable -f\\\" for runtime loading of a new builtin, which can be a shared object that calls setuid() and therefore regains privileges. However, binaries running with an effective UID of 0 are unaffected.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2017-5932\",\"title\":\"The path autocompletion feature in Bash 4\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463439+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"The path autocompletion feature in Bash 4.4 allows local users to gain privileges via a crafted filename starting with a \\\" (double quote) character and a command substitution metacharacter.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2016-9401\",\"title\":\"popd in bash might allow local users to bypass the restricted shell and cause a use-after-free via a...\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463376+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"popd in bash might allow local users to bypass the restricted shell and cause a use-after-free via a crafted address.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2016-7543\",\"title\":\"Bash\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463324+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Bash before 4.4 allows local users to execute arbitrary commands with root privileges via crafted SHELLOPTS and PS4 environment variables.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2014-7187\",\"title\":\"Off-by-one error in the read_token_word function in parse\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463203+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Off-by-one error in the read_token_word function in parse.y in GNU Bash through 4.3 bash43-026 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (out-of-bounds array access and application crash) or possibly have unspecified other impact via deeply nested for loops, aka the \\\"word_lineno\\\" issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2014-7186\",\"title\":\"The redirection implementation in parse\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.463116+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"The redirection implementation in parse.y in GNU Bash through 4.3 bash43-026 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (out-of-bounds array access and application crash) or possibly have unspecified other impact via crafted use of here documents, aka the \\\"redir_stack\\\" issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2014-6277\",\"title\":\"GNU Bash\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462759+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"GNU Bash through 4.3 bash43-026 does not properly parse function definitions in the values of environment variables, which allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (uninitialized memory access, and untrusted-pointer read and write operations) via a crafted environment, as demonstrated by vectors involving the ForceCommand feature in OpenSSH sshd, the mod_cgi and mod_cgid modules in the Apache HTTP Server, scripts executed by unspecified DHCP clients, and other situations in which setting the environment occurs across a privilege boundary from Bash execution.  NOTE: this vulnerability exists because of an incomplete fix for CVE-2014-6271 and CVE-2014-7169.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2012-6711\",\"title\":\"A heap-based buffer overflow exists in GNU Bash\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462426+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"A heap-based buffer overflow exists in GNU Bash before 4.3 when wide characters, not supported by the current locale set in the LC_CTYPE environment variable, are printed through the echo built-in function. A local attacker, who can provide data to print through the \\\"echo -e\\\" built-in function, may use this flaw to crash a script or execute code with the privileges of the bash process. This occurs because ansicstr() in lib/sh/strtrans.c mishandles u32cconv().\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2012-3410\",\"title\":\"Stack-based buffer overflow in lib/sh/eaccess\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462319+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Stack-based buffer overflow in lib/sh/eaccess.c in GNU Bash before 4.2 patch 33 might allow local users to bypass intended restricted shell access via a long filename in /dev/fd, which is not properly handled when expanding the /dev/fd prefix.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2010-0002\",\"title\":\"The /etc/profile\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462246+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"The /etc/profile.d/60alias.sh script in the Mandriva bash package for Bash 2.05b, 3.0, 3.2, 3.2.48, and 4.0 enables the --show-control-chars option in LS_OPTIONS, which allows local users to send escape sequences to terminal emulators, or hide the existence of a file, via a crafted filename.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2008-5374\",\"title\":\"bash-doc 3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"bash\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462164+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"bash-doc 3.2 allows local users to overwrite arbitrary files via a symlink attack on a /tmp/cb#####.? temporary file, related to the (1) aliasconv.sh, (2) aliasconv.bash, and (3) cshtobash scripts.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-6557\",\"title\":\"The MOTD update script in the base-files package in Ubuntu 18\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"base-files\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462097+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"The MOTD update script in the base-files package in Ubuntu 18.04 LTS before 10.1ubuntu2.2, and Ubuntu 18.10 before 10.1ubuntu6 incorrectly handled temporary files. A local attacker could use this issue to cause a denial of service, or possibly escalate privileges if kernel symlink restrictions were disabled.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2010-0834\",\"title\":\"The base-files package\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"base-files\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T10:08:04.462001+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"The base-files package before 5.0.0ubuntu7.1 on Ubuntu 9.10 and before 5.0.0ubuntu20.10.04.2 on Ubuntu 10.04 LTS, as shipped on Dell Latitude 2110 netbooks, does not require authentication for package installation, which allows remote archive servers and man-in-the-middle attackers to execute arbitrary code via a crafted package.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-9232\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-9232 affecting package openssl for versions less than 3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"openssl\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.293302+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-9232 affecting package openssl for versions less than 3.3.5-1. An upgraded version of the package is available that resolves this issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-9230\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-9230 affecting package openssl for versions less than 3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"openssl\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.293194+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-9230 affecting package openssl for versions less than 3.3.5-1. An upgraded version of the package is available that resolves this issue.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-61985\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-61985 affecting package openssh for versions less than 9\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"openssh\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.291164+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-61985 affecting package openssh for versions less than 9.8p1-5. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-61984\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-61984 affecting package openssh for versions less than 9\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"openssh\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.291103+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-61984 affecting package openssh for versions less than 9.8p1-5. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-8291\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-8291 affecting package python3 for versions less than 3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"python3\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.290858+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-8291 affecting package python3 for versions less than 3.12.9-5. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-13601\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-13601 affecting package glib for versions less than 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"glib\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.277846+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-13601 affecting package glib for versions less than 2.78.6-5. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-14087\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-14087 affecting package glib for versions less than 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"glib\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.272343+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-14087 affecting package glib for versions less than 2.78.6-6. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-14512\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-14512 affecting package glib for versions less than 2\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"glib\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.272281+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-14512 affecting package glib for versions less than 2.78.6-6. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-14177\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-14177 affecting package php for versions less than 8\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"php\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.265863+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-14177 affecting package php for versions less than 8.3.29-1. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-14178\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-14178 affecting package php for versions less than 8\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"php\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.265803+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-14178 affecting package php for versions less than 8.3.29-1. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2025-14180\",\"title\":\"CVE-2025-14180 affecting package php for versions less than 8\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"php\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:04.265743+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"CVE-2025-14180 affecting package php for versions less than 8.3.29-1. A patched version of the package is available.\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-1000654\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libtasn1\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:01.523024+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2018-6003\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libtasn1\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:01.522994+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2017-10790\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libtasn1\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:01.522967+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libtasn1 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2019-17498\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libssh2 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libssh2\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:01.522939+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libssh2 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2019-13115\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libssh2 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libssh2\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:01.522913+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libssh2 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2019-3863\",\"title\":\"Security fix for libssh2 in Alpine Linux v3\",\"count\":1,\"active_affected_resources\":[\"libssh2\"],\"match_type\":\"potential\",\"date\":\"2026-04-20T09:24:01.522887+00:00\",\"source\":\"CVE Database\",\"description\":\"Security fix for libssh2 in Alpine Linux v3.18\"},{\"cve_id\":\"CVE-2